# The self-tests that only CI's iOS job (and the gate's iOS steps) run; the group `tooling` is in
# scripts/checks/self-tests-tooling.list (scripts/checks/self-tests.sh reads both). scripts/pre-push-check.sh reads the
# lists (one gate step per line) and CI runs them through one step per job (scripts/checks/self-tests.sh --run <group>).
# `scripts/checks/self-tests.sh --check` fails when a script that has a --self-test is in neither list, or a line names
# a script that is missing or has none. A change to this file is a heavy change (scripts/classify-changes.sh): the iOS
# job reads it; a change to the tooling list is not.
#
# Format: <group> <TAB> <step name> <TAB> <script>   (the step runs `<script> --self-test`)
# Groups, by where each self-test runs:
#   tooling        the gate, always; CI's `tooling` job   (listed in self-tests-tooling.list)
#   macos          the gate, always; CI's `ios-main` job
#   ios-swiftlint  the gate's iOS steps, when swiftlint is installed; CI's `ios-main` job
macos	production framework check self-test	scripts/check-production-framework.sh
ios-swiftlint	localized strings rules self-test	scripts/check-localized-strings.sh
ios-swiftlint	optional_try rule self-test	scripts/check-optional-try.sh
